    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever had a cold or flu that was gone, but the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "cough",
            "ref": "v-cough"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " stayed for weeks? You’re not alone. Many people experience this."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Doctors say some patients cough for up to eight weeks even after the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "virus",
            "ref": "v-virus"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " has left their bodies. “We can’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "detect",
            "ref": "v-detect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the virus anymore, yet they’re still coughing,” says expert Michael Shilho."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Why does this happen? Scientists are still studying it. They believe it has to do with "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "nerves",
            "ref": "v-nerve"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in our "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "airways",
            "zh": "气道"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Coughing is a natural "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "reflex",
            "zh": "反射"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that protects our throat from water or food. When nerves in the airway sense something "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "irritating",
            "ref": "v-irritating"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", they "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "signal",
            "ref": "v-signal"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the brain to cough."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "During an "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "infection",
            "ref": "v-infection"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", our airways become "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "inflamed",
            "zh": "发炎的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This makes the nerves extra sensitive. Even after we recover, these nerves may stay overly reactive for some time."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As researcher Lorcan McGarvey explains, simple actions like breathing deeply, laughing, or going out into cold air—things that aren’t harmful—can "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "trigger"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " coughing long after the illness is over."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In short, a lasting cough doesn’t always mean you’re still sick. It may just be your body’s nerves taking time to calm down."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
